CM_ "BMW E9x M3 ABS/DSC module (Continental MK60E5, software 7846816A). Node DSC = this module. Every frame of the firmware's message tables is listed with every field: fields the firmware discards and transmitted fields with a fixed value are included and say so. Scaling is given where it is established; other fields are raw. Derived from the decompiled firmware, not from a bus capture. Byte/bit numbering 0-based, little-endian (Intel). Fault references are the BMW DTC numbers. Bus: F-CAN (chassis CAN, 500 kbit/s) to the steering-angle sensor and the yaw/acceleration sensor cluster.";
CM_ BO_ 128 "Commands from DSC to the sensor cluster and the steering-angle sensor (BMW: SYNC, DTC C99B on the receiving side): cluster self-test requests, steering-sensor calibration / coding commands, fault-memory clear and the cluster supply state. Sent from its own time slot every 10 ms. Sent by this module, every 10 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 206 "The four wheel speeds, same content as PT-CAN 0x0CE (there every 20 ms). Signed: negative while the wheel direction is known and backward. Magnitude limited to 300 km/h. Sent by this module, every 10 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 286 "Control interventions DSC -> active steering (AFS). In the transmit table with a 10 ms period, but this firmware holds the record off every cycle: never sent (the M3 has no active steering). Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 304 "Terminal (ignition) status: the PT-CAN 0x130 frame of the car access system, forwarded unchanged to F-CAN by the DSC as it is received (about every 100 ms). Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 884 "Learned wheel (tyre) tolerance trims, same content as PT-CAN 0x374. Sent by this module, every 1000 ms.";
CM_ BO_ 1936 "Peer exchange: yaw reference, master-cylinder pressure and two flag bytes. Part of the peer exchange with an external F-CAN brake-request module, which the stock calibration switches off: not on the bus with the stock image. Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 1937 "Peer exchange: steering angle and sensor samples; 0xFFFF for an invalid value. Part of the peer exchange with an external F-CAN brake-request module, which the stock calibration switches off: not on the bus with the stock image. Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 1943 "Peer exchange: the four modelled wheel pressures (all 0xFF while blanked). Part of the peer exchange with an external F-CAN brake-request module, which the stock calibration switches off: not on the bus with the stock image. Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 1944 "Peer exchange: the four wheel speeds (all 0xFF while blanked). Part of the peer exchange with an external F-CAN brake-request module, which the stock calibration switches off: not on the bus with the stock image. Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 2004 "Continental-internal transmit record of the F-CAN table (event). Not sent in any simulated drive; payload not decoded. Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 2005 "Continental-internal transmit record of the F-CAN table (event). Not sent in any simulated drive; payload not decoded. Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 2006 "Continental-internal transmit record of the F-CAN table (event). Not sent in any simulated drive; payload not decoded. Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 2007 "Continental-internal transmit record of the F-CAN table (event). Not sent in any simulated drive; payload not decoded. Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 2008 "Continental-internal transmit record of the F-CAN table (event). Not sent in any simulated drive; payload not decoded. Sent by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 200 "Steering wheel angle frame of the steering-column module. The DSC does not evaluate it; it forwards the frame unchanged to PT-CAN under the same ID. Together with 0x0C9 it is supervised (DTC D373). Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 201 "Steering-angle sensor frame for the DSC: angle, a second (complement) angle, status fields, alive counter and multiplexed service data. The source of the steering angle for AYC and of PT-CAN 0x0C4. No checksum; a repeated alive counter or 15 is an error. Times out after 100 ms (DTC D373); a frame judged implausible does not reload the timeout. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 205 "Yaw/acceleration sensor cluster, channel set A: yaw rate, a supervision word and lateral acceleration, with status, alive counter and CRC-8. The source of yaw and ay. A repeated counter or bad CRC rejects the frame; times out after 100 ms (DTC D370). Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 209 "Sensor cluster, channel set B: two supervision words and the longitudinal acceleration, with status, counter and CRC-8. Times out after 100 ms (DTC D371). Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 212 "Sensor cluster status: status nibbles, status bytes and the flags with which the cluster answers the self-test requests of 0x080. Times out after 100 ms (DTC D372). Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 280 "Active steering (AFS) -> DSC exchange (DTC D375). Received; every field is discarded and a timeout has no effect (the M3 has no active steering). Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 287 "Active steering (AFS) status (DTC D376). Received; every field is discarded and a timeout has no effect. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 320 "Sensor cluster identification: one 16-bit value, stored; reception marks the cluster as present. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 404 "Cruise-control stalk. The DSC does not evaluate it; it forwards the frame unchanged to PT-CAN under the same ID. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 470 "Steering-wheel audio and telephone buttons. The DSC does not evaluate it; it forwards the frame unchanged to PT-CAN under the same ID. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 473 "Steering-wheel M-Drive button. The DSC does not evaluate it; it forwards the frame unchanged to PT-CAN under the same ID. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 678 "Wiper switch. Its mode feeds brake-disc drying. Also forwarded unchanged to PT-CAN under the same ID. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 1934 "Peer exchange: four wheel brake-pressure request channels, handed to the pressure arbiter. Part of the peer exchange with an external F-CAN brake-request module, which the stock calibration switches off: not on the bus with the stock image. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 1935 "Peer exchange: request value, flags and per-channel modes. Ten missed frames count a peer error. Part of the peer exchange with an external F-CAN brake-request module, which the stock calibration switches off: not on the bus with the stock image. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 2012 "Continental-internal receive record of the F-CAN table. Payload not decoded. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 2013 "Continental-internal receive record of the F-CAN table. Payload not decoded. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 2014 "Continental-internal receive record of the F-CAN table. Payload not decoded. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ BO_ 2015 "Continental-internal receive record of the F-CAN table. Payload not decoded. Received by this module, event-driven.";
CM_ SG_ 128 ClusterYawTestRequest "1 while the yaw-rate self-test of the sensor cluster is requested; the cluster answers in 0x0D4.";
CM_ SG_ 128 ClusterAccelTestRequest "1 while the acceleration self-test of the sensor cluster is requested; the cluster answers in 0x0D4.";
CM_ SG_ 128 ClusterTestSpare "Always 0.";
CM_ SG_ 128 Spare_b4 "Always 0.";
CM_ SG_ 128 SzlCommand "Steering-sensor command while one is busy: 1 steering-angle calibration (KWP 31 21), 2 write the sensor's coding byte (KWP 2E 30 01). Held until the sensor reports it in 0x0C9 or 26 cycles.";
CM_ SG_ 128 SzlRoutine2F "2 while the steering-sensor routine 0x2F is requested (after an NM wake-up, a distance reset or a long standstill), otherwise 1.";
CM_ SG_ 128 SzlClearAll "Set for 5 frames after a full fault-memory clear (KWP 14 FF FF).";
CM_ SG_ 128 SzlClearSlots "Set for 5 frames after the second fault-memory clear phase (KWP 14 FF FE).";
CM_ SG_ 128 Spare_b22 "Always 3.";
CM_ SG_ 128 ClusterSupply "1 once the sensor cluster's supply is up and its start-up silence is over; 2 before that or with the supply low.";
CM_ SG_ 128 Spare_b26 "Always 0x3F.";
CM_ SG_ 128 SzlCommandArgument "Argument of SzlCommand: the calibration argument byte or the coding byte, otherwise 0.";
